# Recorded wallet state. Two rungs are committed; the rest are not.
#
# The small ones are here so CI can measure a POPULATED wallet. An empty wallet
# boots fast however badly storage scales, so a runner without fixtures would
# report green having checked the one case that cannot fail. Together they are
# about 66KB in git, and the source hash means a schema change turns CI red
# until someone with the local stack re-records them — which is the correct
# behaviour, and the cost of having them.
#
# The larger rungs stay local. Their value is the cost SHAPE, which needs the
# full ladder, and a 500-coupon fixture is several megabytes of state that is
# re-recorded far more often than it would be reviewed.
*
!.gitignore
!coupons-5.json
!coupons-20.json
